  "body": "Replaces #952: the same commits, moved to a branch in this repository, stacked on #1395; merges after it. Still a draft, held for the PathPilot Hub run.\n\n**Stacked on #951** (#885, branch `issue/885-rotary-feed-cap`): this branch starts from #951's head 83cf9c6b, so its diff here shows #951's commit too until #951 merges. Review only ce987857. Fork synced at v0.17.0.\n\n## What changed\n- `assets/posts/doosan-dnm.cps`: the modal angle memory (`lastA/B/C`) starts as unknown (`null`) and resets to unknown, not 0, at every tool change and section end. The first tilted block of a program and of each section now writes its A word, A0 included, with the M11/M10 brake pair around it. Before, an A0 operation after an A30 one posted no A word and cut at A30.\n- Side effect, kept: with TCP (G43.4) the arm block already wrote A/B/C, but the brake was judged against the assumed A0, so the turn back to A0 ran clamped. That turn now gets M11/M10 too.\n- `crates/app/tests/doosan_dnm_a_state.rs` (new suite, kept out of `doosan_dnm_post.rs`, which would have gone past 400 lines).\n- `crates/app/tests/rotary_feed_cap.rs`: `doosan_fourth_axis_composite_feed_holds_the_stated_a_rate` used to expect the \"angle the post does not know\" refusal for a stream whose opening rapid is at A0. The rapid now writes A0 and places the table, so the test now expects a clean post with `G00 X10 Y0 Z5 A0` and the stated rate held on all 5 turning feeds.\n- `docs/decisions/950-dnm-a-state.md`\n\n**This changes posted G-code** (doosan-dnm.cps, rotary programs only). It waits on a Hub run before it goes ready.\n\n## How tested\n- Pinning tests: `doosan_dnm_a_state::doosan_dnm_writes_a0_after_an_a30_tool` (the issue's two-tool stream, on a no-TCP 4th axis and on the shipped G43.4 DNM machine) and `doosan_dnm_a_state::doosan_dnm_writes_the_opening_a0_without_tcp`. Both fail with the .cps change reverted and pass with it.\n- Local gate (macOS, the worktree's own target, sccache): `cargo test -p camcraft-post` passed. These app binaries passed: doosan_dnm_post 7, doosan_dnm_a_state 2, rotary_feed_cap 5, fourth_axis_pose 9, conformance 6, post_unit_word 5, per_op_files 9, comment_escape 3, suppressed_rest 2. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --tests -- -D warnings` was clean.\n- Goldens moved: **none**. No committed golden is posted through doosan-dnm with an A word.\n\n## Not exercised\n- Real-machine and Hub simulation runs. The full batch tier was not run.\n\nChangelog: doosan-dnm post writes the first A word of every operation (A0 included) instead of assuming the table stands at A0, so an A0 operation after a tilted one no longer cuts at the old angle (#950)\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #950\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n",
